[1m1. Locale-dependent decimal point[22m ([38;5;10mtranslation/src/lib.rs[0m)[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The C library is compiled with [38;5;10m-DENABLE_LOCALES[0m (CMake's [38;5;10mENABLE_LOCALES[0m defaults to [38;5;10mON[0m), so [38;5;10mget_decimal_point()[0m reads [38;5;10mlocaleconv()->decimal_point[0][0m. The Rust version hardcoded [38;5;10mb'.'[0m with a comment claiming locales were off. Under [38;5;10mde_DE.utf8[0m, [38;5;10mcJSON_Parse("1.5")[0m produced [38;5;10m1.5[0m in C but [38;5;10m1.0[0m in Rust (the C code rewrites [38;5;10m.[0m to [38;5;10m,[0m before calling [38;5;10mstrtod[0m, and rewrites it back when printing).[0m[0m
