[1m2. [38;5;10m(int)double[0m conversion of NaN[22m[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10mparse_number[0m, [38;5;10mcJSON_SetNumberHelper[0m and [38;5;10mcJSON_CreateNumber[0m all guard the cast with [38;5;10mnum >= INT_MAX[0m / [38;5;10mnum <= (double)INT_MIN[0m, but NaN fails both comparisons and falls through to the bare cast. On x86-64 [38;5;10mcvttsd2si[0m yields [38;5;10mINT_MIN[0m; Rust's [38;5;10mas[0m is saturating and yields [38;5;10m0[0m. So [38;5;10mcJSON_CreateNumber(NAN)->valueint[0m was [38;5;10m0[0m instead of [38;5;10m-2147483648[0m. Added a [38;5;10mdouble_to_int()[0m helper reproducing the hardware semantics and used it at all three sites.[0m[0m
